1. Complete Customer 360
MATCH (c:Customer {customerId:'C001'})
OPTIONAL MATCH (c)-[r]-(n)
RETURN c,r,n

2. Customers Sharing Same Address
MATCH (c1:Customer)-[:LIVES_AT]->(a:Address)<-[:LIVES_AT]-(c2:Customer)
WHERE c1.customerId <> c2.customerId
RETURN c1.name,c2.name,a.addressLine

Graph version:
MATCH p=(c1:Customer)-[:LIVES_AT]->(a:Address)<-[:LIVES_AT]-(c2:Customer)
WHERE c1.customerId <> c2.customerId
RETURN p

3. Customers Sharing Phone Number
MATCH (c1:Customer)-[:HAS_PHONE]->(p:Phone)<-[:HAS_PHONE]-(c2:Customer)
WHERE c1 <> c2
RETURN c1,c2,p

Graph version:
MATCH path=(c1:Customer)-[:HAS_PHONE]->(phone:Phone)<-[:HAS_PHONE]-(c2:Customer)
WHERE c1 <> c2
RETURN path

4. Related Customers Within 3 Hops
MATCH p=(c:Customer {customerId:'C001'})-[*1..3]-(related)
RETURN p

This is one of the strongest Neo4j demo queries.

5. Most Connected Customers
MATCH (c:Customer)
RETURN c.name,
       COUNT { (c)--() } AS connections
ORDER BY connections DESC

6. Fraud Detection Query
MATCH
(c1:Customer)-[:HAS_PHONE|HAS_EMAIL|LIVES_AT]->(x)<-
[:HAS_PHONE|HAS_EMAIL|LIVES_AT]-(c2:Customer)

WHERE c1 <> c2

RETURN
c1.name,
c2.name,
count(x) AS sharedAttributes
ORDER BY sharedAttributes DESC
